1
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:06,280
Taming The Husband

2
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,920
Episode 5

3
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:14,280
Virtue sustains all things

4
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:21,080
A promise worth its weight in gold
Countless sails have passed

5
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,360
True leisure is a carefree heart
A quiet heart finds contentment

6
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:37,440
Madam. My lady has dealt with the matter.

7
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:40,160
The fourth young master must copy
the household rules 100 times.

8
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,760
Lady Jin is confined for half a month.

9
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:45,360
I didn't want to trouble you,

10
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:46,800
but my lady

11
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:47,880
made a point of sending someone

12
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:49,360
to let you know.

13
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:52,280
She said if you think
anything should be changed,

14
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:53,800
you need only say the word.

15
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,280
She'll do as you wish.

16
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:58,920
So that's why there was shouting

17
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,840
in the other courtyard this morning.

18
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:03,960
That ill-matched pair Lady Qin chose

19
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:07,560
are like two firecrackers tied together.

20
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:11,440
I can't tell if that's good or bad.

21
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:15,400
Now, Madam,
don't trouble yourself over them.

22
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:17,680
The children will find their own way.

23
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,480
It's time you enjoyed a little peace.

24
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:23,760
We're never satisfied, are we?

25
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:26,800
Before Lady Jin married in,

26
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:30,480
I thought Yan was like a stagnant pool.

27
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:35,360
Now he's positively boiling over!

28
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:38,160
New Year's Eve is only a few days away.

29
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,120
First Master Xie and Second Master Xie

30
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:41,560
will both be home for the New Year.

31
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:43,200
This place

32
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:44,680
will be lively then, won't it?

33
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,960
Why wait till New Year's Eve?

34
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:51,600
It's quite lively enough already.

35
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,400
Miss Xi.
The lady of the house punished Lady Jin.

36
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,000
She's confined for half a month.

37
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,560
You mean

38
00:02:58,680 --> 00:02:59,760
Matron Fang

39
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:01,400
will have only me to teach now?

40
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:02,480
Yes, Miss Xi.

41
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:06,360
Xi, make the most of her absence.

42
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:07,600
Show Matron Fang

43
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:09,400
just how well you can do.

44
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:10,760
Of course.

45
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:12,840
I'll make sure she notices me.

46
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,760
Mother, have a cherry.

47
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,080
Speaking of Yingtao,

48
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:22,000
she ruins everything she touches.

49
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:23,560
A born servant, through and through.

50
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:25,640
If she hadn't given us away,

51
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:29,480
we could have won that village girl over.

52
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:31,600
-Exactly.
-She's only a maid.

53
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,960
Why waste your breath on her?

54
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,840
Xie Yan's the one who matters.

55
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:36,960
He may not be able to walk,

56
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:39,200
but there's nothing wrong with his mind.

57
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:42,600
My dear brother,
don't be so hard on yourself.

58
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:43,960
You're quite something, too.

59
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:46,080
Getting it wrong every single time

60
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:47,880
is no easy feat.

61
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:51,960
If you hadn't made
all those stupid blunders,

62
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:54,080
my plan would've worked.

63
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:56,560
Ask Jin Baozhu
for a pig's brain to replace yours.

64
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,680
-What did you say?
-Enough.

65
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:01,880
Both of you, remember this.

66
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:03,560
You're children of the same mother.

67
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:05,360
Stop fighting over outsiders.

68
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:07,560
What matters now is finding a way
to put them in their place.

69
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,760
-Focus on that.
-Don't worry, Mother.

70
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:12,280
I have a very special gift ready.

71
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:15,280
She just has to open it.

72
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:21,920
How's that?

73
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:23,560
-Good. Good.
-That's fine.

74
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,400
-All right.
-Make sure it's straight.

75
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:31,200
What's your business here?

76
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:34,640
My name is Jin Baoyu.

77
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:37,000
Your second young master's
favorite concubine,

78
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:38,280
Jin Baozhu, is my sister.

79
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:40,080
Mother misses her,

80
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:42,240
so she sent me with a few things.

81
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,200
Don't be alarmed, Sir.
First Master Xie brought this

82
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:58,640
chiming clock back from the West.

83
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:00,840
Every hour, it strikes.

84
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:02,440
You'll soon get used to it.

85
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:05,080
A chiming clock?
I know what it is.

86
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:06,360
This way, sir.

87
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:12,840
That's a rich family for you.

88
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:26,080
Baozhu! All the way here,

89
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:27,560
everywhere I went,

90
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,160
the underfloor heating was on full blast.

91
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:31,880
It's the dead of winter,
and I was sweating!

92
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,000
No wonder the windows are all open.

93
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:36,760
By the way, I ran into your husband
on my way here.

94
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:39,000
He must feel the cold, being so frail.

95
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:40,880
He had his page shut the door.

96
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,200
What are you doing here?

97
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,600
You've been married for days,

98
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:47,800
and you still haven't been home.
Your mother misses you.

99
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:51,000
Since it's nearly New Year,
she sent me with some eggs.

100
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:54,440
But looking at you now, it seems you…

101
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:07,480
Look at you, making such a fuss!

102
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:11,920
You've married into a family like this,

103
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,960
and you're drooling over a few eggs?
Have some water.

104
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:17,080
Jin Baozhu, Jin Baozhu.

105
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:20,280
You really have landed on your feet.

106
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:27,160
You can have all this good fortune.
Want it?

107
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:29,080
If you're so keen,

108
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:31,560
cut your precious parts off
and marry in yourself.

109
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:34,760
I'll go and study instead.
And another thing.

110
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:36,360
What were you yelling about out there?

111
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:40,480
What do you want? Out with it, or get out.

112
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:42,800
Nothing much, really.

113
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:45,000
The spring examinations are coming,

114
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:47,080
and I need money for the journey.

115
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:50,080
The money I had
all went on pulling strings.

116
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:53,640
I'm still short this much.

117
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:56,200
Thirty taels? Are you robbing me?

118
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:58,320
Three hundred.

119
00:07:02,080 --> 00:07:03,480
Have you lost your mind?

120
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:04,960
Baozhu, it sounds like a lot,

121
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,240
but to the Xies,

122
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:08,560
it's a drop in the bucket.

123
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:12,680
Look. All these fine things

124
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,800
belong to the Xies.

125
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:16,400
Give them to me,

126
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:19,240
and they belong to the Jins.

127
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,200
Not a chance!

128
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:29,320
Those exams are held every three years.

129
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:31,280
You failed last year.
What exam could you be taking now?

130
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:32,720
Tell me the truth,

131
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:34,080
-or you'll be sorry.
-I'll tell you! I'll tell you!

132
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:36,480
I'll talk!
I'll talk, all right?

133
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:39,000
The moon shines bright

134
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:44,200
It's hot. Open the door.

135
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:45,320
Yes, my lord.

136
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:59,200
My lord, Lady Jin's outside.

137
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:00,280
She seems to want a word.

138
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:01,440
Shall I ask her in?

139
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:02,640
She's got hands and feet.

140
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,280
She can come in and speak for herself.

141
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:08,600
It's cold. Shut the door.

142
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:09,880
Yes, my lord.

143
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,800
What could she want to say?

144
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:26,520
She's such a nuisance.

145
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:28,800
Not a moment's peace, all day long.

146
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:45,280
Please, there's an emergency at home.

147
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:47,080
Can't you two make an exception?

148
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:49,800
Please, my lady.
It's not that we want to stop you,

149
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,040
but if you leave through this gate,

150
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,920
we'll be held responsible.

151
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,960
If you climbed over a low wall,

152
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:57,080
we could look the other way.

153
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,880
I don't know which idiot

154
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,880
put pottery shards all along the walls.

155
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,400
They weren't there before.

156
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:06,960
You're blaming the wrong person.

157
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:09,200
It's Lady Jin you should blame.

158
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:10,280
If she hadn't climbed out

159
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:12,080
to drag someone back
on her wedding night,

160
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:13,760
not only would there be no shards,

161
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,280
but we wouldn't be stuck standing guard.

162
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:26,600
Master Song. Forgive me, Master Song.

163
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:28,200
Could you do us a favor?

164
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:30,480
Last time,
you got us medicine for diarrhea.

165
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:32,280
Two doses, and it worked like a charm.

166
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:34,000
The other guards here

167
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,680
stand out in the cold all year round.

168
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,160
Most of them have the same trouble.

169
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:39,680
They saw how well it worked
and wanted mine.

170
00:09:39,760 --> 00:09:42,360
I couldn't very well say no,
so I gave it all away.

171
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,200
Since you're always
shopping for Lady Qin,

172
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:47,760
could you also
pick up a few doses for the others?

173
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:49,480
We'll pay for the medicine, of course,

174
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:51,560
and a little extra for your trouble.

175
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:53,520
I'll take the cost of the medicine,

176
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:55,000
but there's no need for anything extra.

177
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:56,800
We're all trying to make a living here.

178
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:57,960
No need to stand on ceremony.

179
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:00,880
One more thing.
Some people run cold, others hot.

180
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:03,080
If anyone else asks you for medicine,

181
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:04,360
tell them

182
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:05,680
treatment has to suit the patient.

183
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:08,000
The wrong medicine could make it worse.

184
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,480
Thank you, Master Song.

185
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:11,600
-Here's the medicine you wanted.
-Thank you. Thank you.

186
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:13,480
Thank you.

187
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:16,560
That's a relief.

188
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:17,720
I'll take a dose as soon as I get back.

189
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:18,800
Me too.

190
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:25,520
-They won't take mine this time!
-Right.

191
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:31,120
The sea embraces all

192
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:38,200
Why do you keep following me?

193
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:41,200
Young master, what's your name?

194
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,480
I'm Song Jingxing.

195
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,040
I'm no young master,

196
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,680
just a humble doctor.

197
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:48,400
Humble? From what I just saw,

198
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:49,680
you're rather well connected.

199
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:53,680
If you remember me,

200
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:56,000
you must also remember
what happened at the Lu estate.

201
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:59,360
I had little choice that day.

202
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:01,680
Thank you for speaking up, Lady Jin.

203
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:04,280
If you really want me to forgive you,

204
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,760
could you do me a favor?

205
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:07,560
I can't help you get out.

206
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:10,480
Don't worry. You won't get the blame.

207
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:12,760
I'll dress as your servant

208
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:14,400
and slip out with the shopping party.

209
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:15,800
Pretend you know nothing about it.

210
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:17,640
I'll go in the fourth watch
and be back in the fifth.

211
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:19,280
I don't have a servant.

212
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:23,080
Then… I'll be your apprentice.

213
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:24,960
I don't have one of those, either.

214
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:27,800
You must have someone to wait on you.

215
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:30,120
Let alone a page.

216
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:31,400
You're lying!

217
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:33,800
You can at least read and write.

218
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:34,920
Even a lout like me has one.

219
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,040
How could you not?

220
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:40,040
Because, like you,

221
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:41,760
I live under someone else's roof

222
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:44,280
and have to keep them happy.

223
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:50,880
You already knew what I wanted,

224
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,200
and you won't help.

225
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,600
Why bring me here, then?

226
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:57,760
What's your name?

227
00:11:58,200 --> 00:11:59,200
Jin Baozhu.

228
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:02,200
What did you do for a living?

229
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:03,280
Butchered pigs.

230
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:06,960
Now I know.

231
00:12:08,040 --> 00:12:09,040
Thank you.

232
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:27,680
Useless wretch! Get out!

233
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:30,880
Mother, your heart is weak.
You mustn't get angry.

234
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:36,760
I sent you to hurry breakfast along.

235
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:38,200
What's taking so long?

236
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,240
If I'd sent a dog,

237
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,280
it would've made it back by now!

238
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:46,040
That letter of recommendation,

239
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,760
do you still want it or not?

240
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:51,080
Instead of fawning over that old hag,

241
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,280
you should try pleasing me.

242
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:04,840
I didn't examine Madam today.

243
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:07,640
I was treating the gatekeepers.
That's what kept me.

244
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:09,800
Please forgive me, Mother.

245
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:14,880
Don't call me Mother.

246
00:13:15,040 --> 00:13:16,680
You're not my flesh and blood.

247
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,600
I pitied you back then,

248
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:20,960
so I took you in as a child.

249
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,800
As for those brutes,

250
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:26,240
every one of them is hideous.

251
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:29,360
If they died,
at least I'd be spared the sight.

252
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:33,600
Next time, choose some presentable ones.

253
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:35,560
They'd be easier on the eye.

254
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:38,600
First Master Xie insists on propriety.

255
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:41,360
If he knew you'd replaced the staff
on a whim,

256
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,280
he might be angry.

257
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:47,840
That's what I mean.

258
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:51,160
Being a woman in this family
is so pathetic.

259
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:53,200
Men have it so much better.

260
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:54,920
The Xie men

261
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,760
spend all their time away on the river.

262
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:01,160
Whether they sleep on grain barges

263
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:03,080
or courtesan boats,

264
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:04,800
who's to know?

265
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:13,200
But me?

266
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:16,280
I only have to glance

267
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,880
at a handsome young man,

268
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:20,480
and you'd think I'd broken heaven's law.

269
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:29,240
I've dyed my nails a thousand times,

270
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:31,080
and watched the color fade as often.

271
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:33,400
Still, there's no one to look at them.

272
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:36,280
Just as well.

273
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:39,080
The color's hideous.

274
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:44,680
This dye has been sitting too long.

275
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,680
No wonder the color
isn't what it should be.

276
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:48,080
It's like brewing medicine.

277
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:50,840
Fresh ingredients work best.

278
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:53,960
Don't we have

279
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:56,000
garden balsam in the back courtyard?

280
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:58,960
Someone just needs to pick it properly.

281
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:02,560
The maids and matrons here

282
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:04,160
are with me all day.

283
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,360
They can't just leave.

284
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:10,480
As for you,
you're buried in your medical books.

285
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,000
That reminds me.

286
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:16,480
Those men at the side gate

287
00:15:16,680 --> 00:15:18,640
sit about doing nothing all day.

288
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:21,080
Tell them to come and pick the flowers.
Go now.

289
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,560
You're very particular, Mother.

290
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,640
Picking them could take a while.

291
00:15:27,280 --> 00:15:28,960
Those men have their duties, too.

292
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:30,680
If someone caught them away for too long,

293
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,440
it could be hard to explain.

294
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:36,400
Very well.

295
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:39,080
Have them pick the flowers
after dark tomorrow.

296
00:15:39,280 --> 00:15:40,680
A little each day

297
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:42,400
won't get in the way of their work.

298
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:44,800
Will that do?

299
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:03,840
This medicine's barely working anymore.

300
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:05,120
Perhaps you're

301
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:06,240
getting better, my lord.

302
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:08,680
Shrew! Shrew!

303
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:10,520
Shrew, come out!

304
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:12,200
Let's have another fight!

305
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:13,960
Where is she?

306
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:15,400
Aren't you too old for this?

307
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:16,800
All you do is fool around.

308
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,480
Yan, I haven't been running wild.

309
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:22,760
The last two times, she didn't fight fair.

310
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:24,200
I'm here to challenge her.

311
00:16:24,440 --> 00:16:25,440
Where's that shrew?

312
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:28,160
Lady Jin is still in confinement.

313
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:30,040
She hasn't had a drop of water.

314
00:16:30,760 --> 00:16:32,560
Her brother brought food.

315
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:33,800
She won't starve.

316
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:35,520
Knowing her,

317
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:36,840
could she really be behaving herself?

318
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:38,360
That doesn't sound right.

319
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:43,280
It's been five or six days.

320
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:46,760
What is she up to?

321
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:48,760
If you have something to report, say it.

322
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:50,800
Otherwise, go back and get some rest.

323
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:52,960
Yan, you wouldn't know this,

324
00:16:53,040 --> 00:16:54,600
but when Father and I went to Nanyang,

325
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:56,120
I heard a strange story.

326
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:57,880
A couple went shopping for clothes.

327
00:16:57,960 --> 00:17:00,160
His wife went to the back to try them on,
but she never came out.

328
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:02,200
Her husband looked, but she was gone.

329
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:04,280
There was nothing he could do.
He went home, full of regret.

330
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:06,840
Ten years later, in the street,

331
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:08,800
he saw a familiar figure.

332
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:09,960
It was his wife.

333
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:11,200
Her arms and legs had been cut off.

334
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:13,320
She was begging in the street.

335
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,440
This isn't Nanyang.

336
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:17,600
So you're a couple then?

337
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:20,840
It hurts!

338
00:17:21,080 --> 00:17:22,680
Can't you find something useful to do?

339
00:17:24,600 --> 00:17:25,600
I refuse to believe

340
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:27,920
a little silence could kill anyone.

341
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,240
Though hunger

342
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,840
certainly could.

343
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,600
Jin Baozhu,
I have a bowl of noodles left.

344
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:44,840
Want it?

345
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:55,480
What a shame to waste hand-rolled noodles.

346
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:58,280
Made with freshly harvested winter wheat.

347
00:17:58,560 --> 00:17:59,600
An old hen and marrow bones,

348
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:01,200
simmered for six hours,

349
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:03,280
just to make this bowl of broth.

350
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,720
Add dried bamboo shoots and shrimp roe,

351
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:08,760
and a palm-sized slab of braised pork,

352
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,480
braised until it melts in your mouth.

353
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:12,560
Give me a sincere apology,

354
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:14,040
and you can have it.

355
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:19,040
I'm sincerely reflecting on my mistakes.
Don't let me keep you.

356
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:23,520
Have it your way.

357
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:26,200
I'd sooner throw it out than feed you!
Jianwei, throw it away.

358
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:29,800
My lord! My lord!
We had these noodles

359
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:31,240
cooked specially, just for us.

360
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:32,320
We even dipped into

361
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:33,680
the public allowance to pay for them.

362
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:35,080
It'd be such a waste.

363
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:36,360
-In any case--
-You mean

364
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:39,000
I can no longer

365
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:41,680
spend as I please, throwing money around?

366
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:43,320
No, no! I mean,

367
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:44,840
we don't know how Lady Jin

368
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:46,000
is getting on in there.

369
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:48,080
She might want some tomorrow.

370
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:49,480
We'll take them back and eat them.

371
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:51,200
Let her beg for food tomorrow.

372
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:09,800
Pork! Pork!

373
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,400
Fresh pork!

374
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:13,720
All done, boss.

375
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:14,960
There. Take it.

376
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:16,920
Good. Thank you.

377
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:19,840
Fresh pork! Come and see!

378
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:23,680
Take your pick.

379
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:27,240
That one, with the fat and lean.

380
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:28,800
-My turn! My turn!
-That's my piece.

381
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:30,320
-Come again!
-That one's tasty.

382
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,520
-How's this piece?
-Good.

383
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:33,600
All right.

384
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:35,560
-Here.
-Is mine ready yet?

385
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:37,200
-Just right.
-I'll be late!

386
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:39,960
Good work takes time. Look.
Clean, isn't it?

387
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:41,320
Here's a nice piece. Take it.

388
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:42,840
-Thanks!
-Take care!

389
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,040
Not a wen more or less. It's all here.

390
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:46,840
Come back to me next time.
I'll give you a discount.

391
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:50,320
All right! Here's your pay for today.
Count it.

392
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,920
-I'm off, boss.
-All right. Take care!

393
00:19:58,440 --> 00:19:59,440
Pork! Pork!

394
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:00,840
Fresh pork!

395
00:20:01,560 --> 00:20:03,720
Where did that boy spring from?

396
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:05,160
Charging so little for his work!

397
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:06,720
How are we supposed to make a living?

398
00:20:07,760 --> 00:20:09,320
Nothing's ever enough for him.

399
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:10,680
He'll work himself to death.

400
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:13,440
He won't live to spend what he earns.

401
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:17,040
Dying with money left to spend?

402
00:20:17,160 --> 00:20:18,240
That's a good death.

403
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:20,800
Being alive with no money?

404
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:22,480
That's no life at all.

405
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:24,040
Distilled spirits

406
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:26,680
What did you say?
You! Stop right there!

407
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:34,880
Stinks of pigs.

408
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:36,400
Disgusting.

409
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:38,240
-Go on, get lost.
-Excuse me!

410
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:40,040
-Coming!
-A bowl of plain noodle with topping.

411
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:41,160
How much?

412
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:43,520
-Six wen altogether.
-Six wen?

413
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:44,960
That's robbery!

414
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:46,560
For a bowl of noodles?

415
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:48,720
The plain noodle soup is two wen.

416
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:49,880
It's the topping that costs more.

417
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:51,000
The pork's freshly butchered over there

418
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:52,160
and brought straight here.

419
00:20:52,240 --> 00:20:54,000
Chopped so fine,
cooked until it's so tender.

420
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:55,760
Four wen is a bargain.

421
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:56,920
Just plain noodle soup, then.

422
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Coming up!

423
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:08,840
Wait.

424
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:12,120
-Yes?
-Forget the noodles.

425
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:13,280
Just the topping.

426
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:15,040
Sir, without noodles,

427
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:16,480
what would I put the topping on?

428
00:21:19,520 --> 00:21:20,520
All right.

429
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:34,400
Sir, a butcher
paid to add a topping to your noodles.

430
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:36,200
He asked me to thank you.

431
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:37,480
Where is he?

432
00:21:37,720 --> 00:21:38,720
Over there.

433
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:40,680
He was right here a moment ago.

434
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:44,200
He went that way.

435
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:07,080
It must have been that young doctor.

436
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:08,600
He led them away for me.

437
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:14,160
Yingtao, get me something to eat.

438
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:15,520
I'm starving.

439
00:22:15,680 --> 00:22:17,080
And bring some water.

440
00:22:17,240 --> 00:22:18,560
I want a bath.

441
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:21,160
Jin Baozhu!

442
00:22:24,320 --> 00:22:25,720
Where have you been running wild now?

443
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:30,040
Baozhu.

444
00:22:30,480 --> 00:22:32,280
I was hard at work at school,

445
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:35,600
but some of my classmates

446
00:22:35,680 --> 00:22:36,840
dragged me to Treasure Bowl.

447
00:22:37,720 --> 00:22:39,440
A gambling house? How dare you!

448
00:22:39,560 --> 00:22:41,840
No, no!
They dragged me there against my will!

449
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:43,720
They kept winning.

450
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:46,680
I… I couldn't resist.

451
00:22:46,840 --> 00:22:49,080
And I was thinking of Auntie Zhao,
working so hard, day and night.

452
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:51,080
I wanted a little money to help out.

453
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:52,160
So I tried a few rounds.

454
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:53,680
At first, I won quite a bit.

455
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:58,960
But then my luck turned, and… and…

456
00:23:02,160 --> 00:23:03,720
You lost the whole bride price,

457
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:06,640
then pledged the family home?

458
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:07,800
What did you say?

459
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,960
The creditors will come
to take the house in a few days.

460
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:11,760
Then all of us will be thrown out,

461
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:13,040
out on the streets on New Year's Eve.

462
00:23:13,120 --> 00:23:14,160
Could you let that happen?

463
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:16,040
I wish you'd all freeze,
or starve to death!

464
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:17,120
Then I'd have some peace.

465
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:22,280
Fine. Let us die.
What about your mother?

466
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:24,120
She worked herself to the bone
raising you.

467
00:23:24,320 --> 00:23:25,440
And now you wish her dead?

468
00:23:25,520 --> 00:23:27,560
Have you no conscience?

469
00:23:28,080 --> 00:23:29,920
That day, you were so desperate
to run off and marry.

470
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:32,000
If Auntie hadn't risked her life
to hold me back,

471
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:33,160
I'd have dragged you home.

472
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:34,440
You wouldn't have any of this.

473
00:23:35,040 --> 00:23:36,600
You think you just got lucky?

474
00:23:38,240 --> 00:23:40,160
We can't even afford to eat.

475
00:23:40,840 --> 00:23:42,000
Did you know

476
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:43,480
Auntie didn't touch

477
00:23:43,560 --> 00:23:44,600
a bite of her own share?

478
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:45,960
She sent it all to you.

479
00:23:46,040 --> 00:23:47,280
So what if I knew?

480
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:48,760
Or if I didn't?

481
00:23:49,560 --> 00:23:51,240
Am I meant to cry for the lot of you?

482
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:53,480
In the three years since Father died,

483
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:54,960
I've worked through wind and rain.

484
00:23:55,080 --> 00:23:57,080
Come hell or high water,
I had to butcher pigs and sell meat.

485
00:23:57,440 --> 00:24:00,160
But you? Perfectly able-bodied,

486
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:02,240
and all living off my back!

487
00:24:02,560 --> 00:24:03,960
When I earned money, you expected it.

488
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:06,080
When I didn't, you made my life miserable.

489
00:24:06,320 --> 00:24:08,880
Tell me, where's my good fortune?

490
00:24:09,080 --> 00:24:10,440
I've had nothing but misery!

491
00:24:10,720 --> 00:24:12,080
After all I've been through,

492
00:24:12,240 --> 00:24:14,840
now you're nice to me for once,

493
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:17,240
bring me a basket of lousy eggs,
and expect me to be grateful?

494
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:21,160
You think I'm some kind of saint
here to save the world?

495
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:29,160
You, all of you deserve it!

496
00:24:29,280 --> 00:24:31,200
Baozhu, I…

497
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:34,640
I'm sorry, Baozhu. I was wrong.

498
00:24:34,720 --> 00:24:36,760
But our family's really reached

499
00:24:36,840 --> 00:24:38,280
the end of the road.

500
00:24:38,720 --> 00:24:40,720
I'm begging you.

501
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:42,080
Help us.

502
00:24:49,040 --> 00:24:50,720
You're supposed to be a scholar.

503
00:24:52,120 --> 00:24:53,720
The family needs you to take the exams.

504
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:56,200
I'll let you off one last time.

505
00:24:57,440 --> 00:24:59,080
Do it again,

506
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:00,800
and I'll chop your hands off.

507
00:25:03,600 --> 00:25:04,680
I won't.

508
00:25:06,160 --> 00:25:07,280
Never again.

509
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:10,000
I took something from the house,
a jade carving, and gave it to him.

510
00:25:10,680 --> 00:25:13,440
So he could
pay off the owner of Treasure Bowl.

511
00:25:14,080 --> 00:25:16,400
Then I'd get out and earn money
butchering pigs.

512
00:25:16,840 --> 00:25:18,720
Once I'd saved enough, I'd buy it back.

513
00:25:18,800 --> 00:25:20,040
You make it sound so simple.

514
00:25:20,760 --> 00:25:22,480
You think we're a market stall?

515
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:25,080
Lose a valuable,
and it's no worse than losing a cabbage?

516
00:25:25,480 --> 00:25:27,640
Everything the Xies own
is listed in a register.

517
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:29,120
You can't just sell it off!

518
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:31,480
And you're still confined.

519
00:25:32,480 --> 00:25:33,600
If anyone finds out,

520
00:25:33,880 --> 00:25:34,880
you'll be punished for both offenses.

521
00:25:35,120 --> 00:25:36,520
You won't escape a beating.

522
00:25:37,280 --> 00:25:39,520
And you'll disgrace me
in front of the whole clan.

523
00:25:39,720 --> 00:25:41,360
Then don't let them find out!

524
00:25:41,440 --> 00:25:43,080
I said I'd buy it back.

525
00:25:43,160 --> 00:25:44,320
Everything the Xies own

526
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:45,600
bears the family seal.

527
00:25:46,040 --> 00:25:47,280
If it ends up in a gambling house,

528
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:49,200
you think no one will find out?

529
00:25:50,160 --> 00:25:51,880
Your family has so many rules.

530
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:54,280
How was I to know? I wanted to ask you,

531
00:25:54,360 --> 00:25:55,440
but you wouldn't see me.

532
00:25:55,520 --> 00:25:56,720
I wouldn't see you

533
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:59,080
because you insulted me

534
00:25:59,600 --> 00:26:00,680
and refused to apologize.

535
00:26:02,800 --> 00:26:03,920
I was wrong about this,

536
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:05,480
but I wasn't wrong about that.

537
00:26:05,560 --> 00:26:06,680
Why should I apologize for that

538
00:26:06,760 --> 00:26:07,880
because of this?

539
00:26:09,680 --> 00:26:11,200
What do you use to sharpen your knives?

540
00:26:11,280 --> 00:26:12,680
A stone. Why?

541
00:26:13,160 --> 00:26:16,000
I thought you used that head of yours.
It's certainly hard enough.

542
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:20,400
So many clever insults,

543
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:22,600
and now you've nothing to say?

544
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:34,040
Let's get the carving back first.

545
00:26:35,080 --> 00:26:36,720
These are my savings for emergencies.

546
00:26:37,640 --> 00:26:39,560
Are you going yourself, my lord?
Let me go.

547
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:41,360
Treasure Bowl's no place for you.

548
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:43,400
Madam would be furious if she found out.

549
00:26:43,480 --> 00:26:45,880
I'm not going. I'd die of shame.

550
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:49,640
Let whoever caused the trouble go.

551
00:27:02,480 --> 00:27:03,480
I'm sorry.

552
00:27:08,120 --> 00:27:09,120
Jianwei.

553
00:27:10,040 --> 00:27:11,280
Keep an eye on her from behind.

554
00:27:11,760 --> 00:27:13,280
Don't let her cause any more trouble.

555
00:27:13,360 --> 00:27:14,360
Yes, my lord.

556
00:27:26,480 --> 00:27:28,520
Someone! The masters are back!

557
00:27:28,600 --> 00:27:29,880
Come and help with the baggage!

558
00:27:30,240 --> 00:27:31,240
Coming!

559
00:27:32,680 --> 00:27:33,680
Come on! Come on!

560
00:27:34,880 --> 00:27:35,880
Let's go.

561
00:27:36,520 --> 00:27:38,120
You're home.

562
00:27:38,240 --> 00:27:40,080
That's all that matters. You're safe.

563
00:27:40,440 --> 00:27:43,160
After a year away,

564
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:45,200
you've both lost weight.

565
00:27:47,480 --> 00:27:48,920
Thank you for your concern, Mother.

566
00:27:49,120 --> 00:27:51,120
I've been well.

567
00:27:52,080 --> 00:27:53,320
On this grain transport run,

568
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:56,240
we expanded our business considerably
along the Huai'an stretch.

569
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:59,120
Revenue is up by more than 30%
on past years.

570
00:27:59,200 --> 00:28:00,560
I've had the accountants

571
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:01,720
prepare a detailed breakdown.

572
00:28:01,800 --> 00:28:03,720
I'll bring it for you to inspect later.

573
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:07,200
Also, I've brought you

574
00:28:07,280 --> 00:28:08,760
a New Year gift.

575
00:28:10,200 --> 00:28:11,640
Passing through Yingtian Prefecture,

576
00:28:11,720 --> 00:28:13,160
I found some fine material

577
00:28:13,320 --> 00:28:15,200
and had a master craftsman
make it into an inkstone.

578
00:28:15,920 --> 00:28:17,920
Colored glass weathers the elements
without decay,

579
00:28:18,080 --> 00:28:20,520
like evergreen pines and cypresses.

580
00:28:20,920 --> 00:28:23,400
May you live a long, happy life, Mother.

581
00:28:24,120 --> 00:28:25,520
How kind of you to remember

582
00:28:25,600 --> 00:28:27,040
an old woman like me.

583
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:29,440
Though

584
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:32,040
I rarely practice calligraphy now.

585
00:28:33,360 --> 00:28:35,400
But these words, "Clear Heart,"

586
00:28:35,640 --> 00:28:38,120
suit Yan's name, Chengjiang,
"Clear River."

587
00:28:38,640 --> 00:28:40,640
Put it in Yan's room.

588
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:43,880
Tell him his father's home

589
00:28:43,960 --> 00:28:45,640
and brought it especially for him.

590
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:47,000
Yes, Madam.

591
00:28:49,680 --> 00:28:52,400
Mother, I'm a rough sort.

592
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:54,120
I've been on the river since I was a boy.

593
00:28:54,280 --> 00:28:55,360
Unlike my younger brother,

594
00:28:55,440 --> 00:28:57,120
I've never served at court.

595
00:28:57,880 --> 00:29:00,080
I don't know how to choose
such exquisite things.

596
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:02,320
In my bags,

597
00:29:02,400 --> 00:29:04,720
you'll find all your favorite foods.

598
00:29:04,800 --> 00:29:06,040
Fragrant rice from Qufu.

599
00:29:06,120 --> 00:29:07,560
Golden-Thread Gourds from Xuzhou.

600
00:29:07,640 --> 00:29:08,840
Chicken cakes from Lianshui.

601
00:29:08,920 --> 00:29:09,960
Salted duck eggs from Gaoyou.

602
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:11,920
Huai'an's crispy fried dough strands
and Shaobo water caltrops.

603
00:29:12,200 --> 00:29:13,400
And your favorite,

604
00:29:13,480 --> 00:29:14,560
lotus root powder from Baoying.

605
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:15,880
My brother entered the trade before me.

606
00:29:15,960 --> 00:29:17,760
All those years on the river

607
00:29:17,840 --> 00:29:20,160
-have made him quite the connoisseur.
-You're too kind.

608
00:29:20,240 --> 00:29:21,440
It's a modest gift,

609
00:29:21,560 --> 00:29:23,560
but it comes from the heart.

610
00:29:24,280 --> 00:29:25,280
Brother.

611
00:29:25,600 --> 00:29:26,600
Too kind. Too kind.

612
00:29:27,400 --> 00:29:29,760
I couldn't possibly eat all of this!

613
00:29:29,840 --> 00:29:30,880
That's all right.

614
00:29:30,960 --> 00:29:34,080
Matron Fang. Send some to each courtyard.

615
00:29:34,520 --> 00:29:35,720
Tell them the masters

616
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:36,800
brought them home,

617
00:29:36,880 --> 00:29:38,720
so everyone can share in the festivities.

618
00:29:39,320 --> 00:29:40,320
Yes, Madam.

619
00:29:45,880 --> 00:29:48,680
Xie Heng, first young master
Lin Chanyue's daughter

620
00:29:48,800 --> 00:29:49,880
Grandmother.

621
00:29:51,520 --> 00:29:52,680
The elders

622
00:29:52,760 --> 00:29:53,800
took such good care of me on the journey.

623
00:29:53,960 --> 00:29:55,320
I learned a great deal.

624
00:29:55,880 --> 00:29:57,360
The scenery was magnificent.

625
00:29:57,600 --> 00:29:59,160
Since you've never traveled so far,

626
00:30:01,200 --> 00:30:02,840
I drew you a waterway chart.

627
00:30:03,560 --> 00:30:06,840
I've marked this year's new
shoals and ports on it.

628
00:30:07,400 --> 00:30:09,440
When the younger ones go to sea,

629
00:30:09,800 --> 00:30:10,960
they'll find it useful, too.

630
00:30:11,640 --> 00:30:14,280
Quick, let me see!

631
00:30:21,800 --> 00:30:23,560
How thoughtful of you.

632
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:25,640
Such fine detail.

633
00:30:26,560 --> 00:30:28,280
With all the jolting on board,

634
00:30:29,280 --> 00:30:31,200
you must take care of your eyes.

635
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:34,880
The Xie family will be counting on

636
00:30:34,960 --> 00:30:36,560
you younger ones

637
00:30:36,680 --> 00:30:38,440
to take it to greater heights.

638
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:42,000
I'll remember your words, Grandmother.

639
00:30:42,200 --> 00:30:43,640
I only did what was expected of me.

640
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:45,080
I take no special credit.

641
00:30:45,400 --> 00:30:48,800
You know, you mustn't sell yourself short.

642
00:30:56,360 --> 00:30:58,200
You're the eldest son of the Xie family.

643
00:31:01,440 --> 00:31:04,480
There's no responsibility beyond you.

644
00:31:14,760 --> 00:31:15,800
Take a good look!

645
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:22,680
Treasure Bowl
Where bold gamblers and heroes gather

646
00:31:23,520 --> 00:31:24,520
Place your bets! Hands off!

647
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:31,160
You're going to lose.

648
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:32,640
Come on, come on!

649
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:33,960
Show us! Show us!

650
00:31:34,040 --> 00:31:35,360
-Baoyu.
-Big!

651
00:31:35,440 --> 00:31:36,440
Leave me alone.

652
00:31:36,600 --> 00:31:38,720
-Baoyu!
-Leave me alone! Let go!

653
00:31:38,800 --> 00:31:41,040
Stop this, Baoyu. Stop gambling.

654
00:31:41,120 --> 00:31:43,200
If you carry on,
you'll ruin the Jin family,

655
00:31:43,280 --> 00:31:44,840
and your sister will never be able to
hold her head up in her new home.

656
00:31:44,920 --> 00:31:46,000
Will you stop pestering me?

657
00:31:46,720 --> 00:31:49,480
Baoyu. I'll get down on my knees. Baoyu!

658
00:31:49,560 --> 00:31:50,640
Has some devil

659
00:31:50,720 --> 00:31:52,080
blinded you, Baoyu?

660
00:31:52,280 --> 00:31:53,320
Stop this, Baoyu!

661
00:31:53,400 --> 00:31:55,040
I'm betting on the banker!

662
00:31:55,120 --> 00:31:56,520
Stop gambling, Baoyu!

663
00:31:56,600 --> 00:31:57,600
Baozhu!

664
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:02,000
Jin Baoyu!

665
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:04,960
Baozhu!
